## Initialization

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
    'PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'parserPopUp.pl', 'scaffold.pl', 'contextFraction.pl',
    'PGcourse.pl'
);

Context("Numeric");
Context()->variables->set(n => "Real");

do {

    $a = random(2, 10);
    $b = random(2, 10);
    $c = non_zero_random(-10, 10, 1);
    $d = non_zero_random(-10, 10, 1);
} until ($a * $d != $b * $c);

$limtest = DropDown(
    [ "greater than 1", "less than 1", "not equal to 0", " equal to 0" ],
    "not equal to 0");
$divconknow1 =
    DropDown([ "the series converges", "the series diverges", "nothing" ],
        "the series diverges");

BEGIN_PGML
Test the series for convergence or divergence.
[``` \sum_{n=11}^\infty  \frac{(-1)^n([$a] n + [$c])}{[$b] n + [$d]}.```]

END_PGML

#  The scaffold
Scaffold::Begin(
    can_open => "when_previous_correct",
    is_open  => "correct_or_first_incorrect"
);

#only the active section is open, but students can open previous sections if they want.

Section::Begin("Part 1: Divergence Test");

$bnans  = Compute("($a n+$c)/($b n + $d)");
Context('Fraction');
$limans = Fraction($a, $b);

BEGIN_PGML

Identify: [`b_n=`] [_]{$bnans}{20}   

Evaluate the limit: [`\displaystyle \lim_{n \to \infty} b_n = `] [_]{$limans}{10}

Since [`\displaystyle \lim_{n \to \infty} b_n `] is [_]{$limtest}
the Divergence Test tells us that [_]{$divconknow1}.

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
The term [`b_n`] is the term without the change in sign so 
[``` b_n = [$bnans] ```]

The limit is found by the ratio of leading terms or 
[``` \lim_{n \to \infty} b_n = [$limans] ```]

Since the limit is *not equal to zero*, the divergence test tells us that *the series diverges*.
END_PGML_SOLUTION

Section::End();

Section::Begin("Part 2: Alternating Series Test");

$divconknow2 = PopUp(
    [ "Select", "the series converges", "the series diverges", "nothing" ],
    "the series diverges"
);

BEGIN_PGML
The Alternating Series Test is unnecessary since the Divergence Test already determined that
[_]{$divconknow2}
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
As the problem states that since the divergence test showed that the series diverges, the alternating series test does not need to be performed.
END_PGML_SOLUTION

Section::End();

Scaffold::End();

ENDDOCUMENT();
